      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.32,
      "end_seconds": 217.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.48,
      "end_seconds": 234.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "There is wheeze at both bases and your oxygen is a little low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.28,
      "end_seconds": 242.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.31,
      "end_seconds": 255.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "having listened and examined, I'd lean towards a flare-up of COPD"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.61,
      "end_seconds": 260.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I mean, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.05,
      "end_seconds": 270.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like a flare-up of COPD, but I'd like to confirm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.0,
      "end_seconds": 318.07,
      "duration_seconds": 32.07,
      "text": "let's book a chest X-ray to look into COPD flare. I'm going to put you on doxycycline 100 milligrams once a day five days. That should help with chest infection. Use your inhaler regularly and get seen if you are not better in three days. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Let's hold off on a sputum sample for now and if there's no change next month we can revisit it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.02,
      "end_seconds": 329.19,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "please don't wait if the symptoms get worse that's when to be seen urgently we'll catch up in one week that's all from me any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.32,
      "end_seconds": 334.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "okay, that that makes sense thanks for explaining"
